[{:db/id "q-20797/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "bce81980-d4c6-51f4-a08b-bace845047cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20797/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "3e8c381f-586b-5a32-a993-8f860bd663d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20797/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "84b84f50-e25f-59d1-89dd-1f9a117bdbb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20797/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "800d37d1-b4ef-5db7-9566-876a4ab33a73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20797/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "ffe2c351-4438-5626-84b7-523a1e0a0461" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20797/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5d0ef435-1c50-5611-bca4-5634a0380660" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-20797/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-20797/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-20797/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-20797/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-20797/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-20797/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-20797" :question/id #uuid "2dfa35ce-beed-58f8-8439-6e601518f0e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-20797" :question/problem "Find the total area of the region bounded by the graph of the curve $y=3{x}^{2}{e}^{-|x{|}^{3}}$ and the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "We find the area of the region bounded by the graph of the curve and the $x$-axis by calculating the integral\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }3{x}^{2}{e}^{-|x{|}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nWe break up the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }3{x}^{2}{e}^{-|x{|}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}3{x}^{2}{e}^{-|x{|}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }3{x}^{2}{e}^{-|x{|}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWe start by calculating the first of these integrals:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}3{x}^{2}{e}^{-|x{|}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}3{x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWe calculate the antiderivative using a substitution. Let $u={x}^{3}$,  then $\\text{d}u=3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Hence, the antiderivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3{x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={e}^{u}+C \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{3}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}3{x}^{2}{e}^{-|x{|}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}3{x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}3{x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{({e}^{{x}^{3}})|}_{a}^{0} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }({e}^{0}-{e}^{{a}^{3}}) \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the integrand $3{x}^{2}{e}^{-|x{|}^{3}}$ is an **even** function. This means that we can immediately deduce that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }3{x}^{2}{e}^{-|x{|}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since both improper integrals exist, we conclude that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }3{x}^{2}{e}^{-|x{|}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}3{x}^{2}{e}^{-|x{|}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }3{x}^{2}{e}^{-|x{|}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1+1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-20797/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d083b53b-8c39-5785-a250-5649001e822b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-20797"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-20804/selection/7ea009d38067b85c260cd71ce15cce585e1f931f7adf440bc470127b22bd36c2" :answer/id #uuid "15bc5a5d-5f32-5827-95aa-cea376046798" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The integral is divergent" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20804/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "1045e7e0-b7da-55ad-be68-d1290286416b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20804/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" :answer/id #uuid "43e22a05-9c84-50a4-a49b-e3b90ffd284e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20804/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "6ebb3d87-0b26-538f-9887-ee0670dee379" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20804/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "5c4fa1cb-a166-5ac0-8db4-342c00bdd9fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20804/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d624deec-d629-5e5a-8626-3caa4566f007" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-20804/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-20804/selection/7ea009d38067b85c260cd71ce15cce585e1f931f7adf440bc470127b22bd36c2" "q-20804/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-20804/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" "q-20804/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-20804/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-20804" :question/id #uuid "68984b43-c28b-51c9-a2e8-e7cd0fb9d27d" :question/math-academy-id "q-20804" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{2x}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We break up the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{2x}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{2x}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{2x}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the antiderivative using a substitution. Let  $u={x}^{2}$,  then $\\text{d}u=2x\\text{d}x.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{9+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\frac{u}{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now evaluate the first of the improper integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{2x}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}\\frac{2x}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{(\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3})|}_{a}^{0} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\frac{{0}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\frac{{a}^{2}}{3}) \\\\  & =-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(0-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\frac{{a}^{2}}{3}) \\\\  & =0-\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the integrand is an **odd** function. This means that we can immediately deduce that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{2x}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since both improper integrals exist, we conclude that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{2x}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{2x}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{2x}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-20804/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fe1f468-9e8d-58fc-bd61-cfe1191a5a19"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-20804"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-30967"] :question/problem "Find the total area of the region bounded by the graph of the curve $y=|x|{e}^{-{x}^{2}}$ and the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "We find the area of the region bounded by the graph of the curve and the $x$-axis by calculating the integral\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }|x|{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe break up the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }|x|{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}|x|{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }|x|{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe start by calculating the first of these integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}|x|{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}x{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the antiderivative using a substitution. Let  $u=-{x}^{2}$,  then $\\text{d}u=-2x\\text{d}x.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{u}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{u}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-{x}^{2}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}|x|{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x & =-{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}x{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}x{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }({-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-{x}^{2}}|}_{a}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }({e}^{0}-{e}^{-{a}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the integrand $|x|{e}^{-{x}^{2}}$ is an **even** function. This means that we can immediately deduce that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }|x|{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since both improper integrals exist, we conclude that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }|x|{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}|x|{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }|x|{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-118776/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "4e831a23-ec58-57c0-b08a-10f1936c0841" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118776/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" :answer/id #uuid "a37aeded-9bcc-5dea-b427-9c06442ba73a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118776/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "5eebd6b6-65b8-5ecb-b8b5-3fed8d561976" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118776/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "4983a346-cbaf-59f1-833e-14e3d492549a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118776/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "eed4fa3d-ca16-5a44-a65e-da0e02f4853c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118776/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b190eda4-0caa-5dc2-a98a-1322d9b66a73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-118776/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-118776/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-118776/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" "q-118776/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-118776/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-118776/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-118776" :question/id #uuid "aa4a3d4f-86d7-526d-8b7d-9356bb095979" :question/math-academy-id "q-118776" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{x}{{(3+{x}^{2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We break up the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{x}{{(3+{x}^{2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{x}{{(3+{x}^{2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{x}{{(3+{x}^{2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the antiderivative using a substitution. Let  $u=3+{x}^{2}$,  then $\\text{d}u=2x\\text{d}x.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x}{{(3+{x}^{2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{u})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2(3+{x}^{2})}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now evaluate the first of the improper integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{x}{{(3+{x}^{2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}\\frac{x}{{(3+{x}^{2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{(-\\frac{1}{2(3+{x}^{2})})|}_{a}^{0} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\frac{1}{2(3+0)}-\\frac{1}{2(3+{a}^{2})}) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{1}{6}-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the integrand is an **odd** function. This means that we can immediately deduce that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{x}{{(3+{x}^{2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since both improper integrals exist, we conclude that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{x}{{(3+{x}^{2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{x}{{(3+{x}^{2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{x}{{(3+{x}^{2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-118776/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fe1f468-9e8d-58fc-bd61-cfe1191a5a19"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-118776"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-118777/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951" :answer/id #uuid "f28539e6-2dbd-58bb-9599-64198317af32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118777/selection/e65264720c59aa6cf4dec4ef6ab354eac2177abff5c6282da5c317519a0708d0" :answer/id #uuid "cd82ee17-fa8c-549c-a03a-f9a0799f9870" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118777/selection/36daa82f4bec5a22e7ba82725971830f1b50dd88483299919d4785b6db46088e" :answer/id #uuid "fd0b8ec2-e548-5200-a362-c9139d70275a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118777/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "0b88e548-8a1e-5925-8aac-99ade3b148d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118777/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" :answer/id #uuid "b5a46bbe-4777-5066-b5a3-5103698bef72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118777/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "93e72a3e-09bd-544e-aa7f-fa5fd9aa8792" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-118777/selection/e65264720c59aa6cf4dec4ef6ab354eac2177abff5c6282da5c317519a0708d0" :answer-field/choices ["q-118777/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951" "q-118777/selection/e65264720c59aa6cf4dec4ef6ab354eac2177abff5c6282da5c317519a0708d0" "q-118777/selection/36daa82f4bec5a22e7ba82725971830f1b50dd88483299919d4785b6db46088e" "q-118777/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-118777/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-118777" :question/id #uuid "e1104938-8add-5c20-aaed-a503fbe2493d" :question/math-academy-id "q-118777" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{9+2{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We break up the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{9+2{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{3}{9+2{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{9+2{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nEvaluating the first of these integrals, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{3}{9+2{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}\\frac{3}{9+2{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{(\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }({\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}x}{3})|}_{a}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡0-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}a}{3})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot [0-(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the integrand is an **even** function. This means that we can immediately deduce that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{9+2{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\pi }{2\\sqrt{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since both improper integrals exist, we conclude that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{9+2{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{3}{9+2{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{9+2{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2\\sqrt{2}}+\\frac{\\pi }{2\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-118777/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fe1f468-9e8d-58fc-bd61-cfe1191a5a19"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-118777"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
